        "original_id": "667fc4a8-759e-50d4-a0e8-6be56f52e24d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gordon Waller, Paul McCartney, Del Davis\n- Music groups: Peter and Gordon\n- Songs: \"A World Without Love\", \"World Without Love\"\n- Albums: \"Mellow Dubmarine\"\n\nFacts:\n- Gordon Waller was a British singer-songwriter-guitarist who was born on 4 June 1945 and died on 17 July 2009.\n- Gordon Waller was best known as Gordon in the 1960s pop duo Peter and Gordon.\n- \"A World Without Love\" was the biggest hit by Peter and Gordon and was a No. 1 million-selling song.\n- Paul McCartney wrote the song \"A World Without Love,\" and it was attributed to Lennon-McCartney.\n- Del Davis recorded a cover of \"World Without Love\" that was featured on the album \"Mellow Dubmarine\".",
